The Text Attribute ID docs:
> Identifies the IsReadOnly text attribute, which indicates whether the text is read-only (TRUE) or can be modified (FALSE).

@codeofdusk made an interesting suggestion as to the interpretation of that text: append "by the user" at the end. In console, a user can interact with the buffer via key strokes, and those key strokes may modify any section of the buffer. Surprisingly, something like "text on a webpage" is also _not_ read only! `IsReadOnly` seems to be limited to text that is disabled and cannot be interacted with in any way.
